    - target: {fileID: 8902907873516035281, guid: 8696efd15abc1d7468b2986604dc05f1, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "\u201CSelect every unique pair of rune stones to moves the stones!\u201D"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9091669035569178768, guid: 8696efd15abc1d7468b2986604dc05f1, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: "That\u2019s Correct!\n\n\u201CThe rune stones were A, B, and C. Since
        we are only selecting pairs and the order does not matter, each pair counts
        as a single result. This is called a combination.\n\nLet\u2019s list all
        possible pairs:\n\nAB, AC, BC\n\nThere are 3 total pairs.\n\nThis can be
        denoted by the following  notations:\n\nnCr \\; C(n, r) \\; C(\\nfrac{n}{r})\n\nAnd
        this can be calculated using the combination formula:\n\nC(n, r) = \\frac{n!}{(n
        - r)! r!}\n\nC(3, 2) = \\frac{3!}{(3 - 2)! 2!} = \\frac{3!}{1! 2!} = \\frac{3!}{2!}
        = \\frac{3x2!}{2!} = 3 ways\n\nThere are 3 possible combinations\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
